~ pantry_filler
% => convo_1
% => convo_2
% => convo_3
% => convo_4
% => convo_5
% => convo_6
=> END

~ convo_1
Az: Ugh, this sucks.
Fenn: Why?
Az: I need to get to my workshop. I hate being stuck.
Fenn: It's okay! I'm here!
Az: That you are...
#do EventFlags.set_flag("F-1-Az-Pantry", true)
=> END

~ convo_2
Fenn: So you made these bangles?
Az: Yeah, why?
Fenn: That's... SO COOL. How did you get these tiny little indents in there?
Az: The... patterns?
Fenn: Whoa.... yeah! The patterns!
Az: I... well, I carved them. It's really not that hard.
Fenn: AWESOME.
#do EventFlags.set_flag("F-2-Az-Pantry", true)
=> END

~ convo_3
Az: I need to get my Baba out of there. 
Fenn: Well, once we defeat Mr. Wizard Man, he'll help us!
Az: He doesn't seem to be in a helping mood, Fenn.
#do EventFlags.set_flag("F-3-Az-Pantry", true)
=> END

~ convo_4
Az: I don't mean to be rude, but, like, why are you here?
Fenn: What do you mean?
Az: In the palace? 
Fenn: Oh! I was invited! Uh... King Oakley sent a letter to me. 
Fenn: He... uh... he's looking for candidates for new Knights!!
=> END

~ convo_5
Fenn: Who's your favorite Knight? Like, besides your Dad?
Az: Hmm... besides Baba? I haven't really spent time with them
Az: Henric and Ophelia are, like, kinda intense. I'd say Maysa. She's chill.
Fenn: Oooh, good choice. I think I have a few Maysas. Mostly Adira and Henric full-arts.
Az: Wait- are you talking about trading cards?
Fenn: Yeah I have a ton of them!
Az: Huh... I didn't know they made trading cards of the Knights.
Fenn: They don't!
Az: Ah...
=> END


~ convo_6
Fenn: Do you like living at the palace?
Az: Eh. It's cool, I guess. I got my own workshop... plenty of stuff to tinker with... all the time in the world.
Az: Not the same as home, though.
Fenn: Kuva, right?
Az: Yeah... how'd you know?
Fenn: It's in your biography at the Grasen History Museum!
Az: Ah... right. 
Fenn: You grew up on Straw Ave, had two best friends, and won crafts shows before getting into smithing! Oh and also, that one ti-
Az: Okay! Okay, that's enough out of you, Fenn.
=> END
